---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/utils';
import Animations from '../../components/Animations.vue';
import CommentsSection from '../../components/CommentsSection.vue';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    { params: { lang: 'en' } },
    { params: { lang: 'es' } },
    { params: { lang: 'pt' } },
  ];
}

const { lang } = Astro.params;
const t = useTranslations(lang);

const content = {
  en: {
    title: "Cloud Cybersecurity and AI — Automation with SecLM and Digital Sovereignty",
    date: "October 4, 2026",
    subtitle: "A developer diary entry by Jill",
    back: 'Back to Home',
    intro: "Understanding how AI models specialized in cybersecurity (SecLM) and digital sovereignty frameworks enhance cloud security operations.",
    introDesc: "A technical overview of automated threat detection, log analysis, and data residency compliance in cloud environments.",
    introExtra: [
      "SecLM is a specialized LLM fine-tuned on Mandiant threat intelligence and Google security telemetry.",
      "Digital sovereignty ensures enterprise data remains within specific geographical jurisdictions under local regulatory compliance."
    ],
    section1: {
      heading: "1. AI in Cloud Security: What Is SecLM?",
      paragraphs: [
        "Modern cloud environments generate millions of security events and log entries daily. Traditional SIEM (Security Information and Event Management) tools rely on static rule sets that often produce high false-positive noise.",
        `**SecLM (Security Language Model)** is a specialized AI model trained on threat analysis reports, malware behavior, and security configurations *(if you want to learn more about specialized local AI models, read my <a href="/en/blog-hermes" class="inline-blog-link">entry on local LLMs and Hermes Agent</a>)*.`,
        "In **Security AI Command Center**, SecLM acts as an automated analyst: translating complex multi-stage attack graphs into natural language summaries and suggesting remediation CLI commands."
      ]
    },
    section2: {
      heading: "2. Digital Sovereignty & Data Residency",
      paragraphs: [
        "As organizations in Latin America and globally move mission-critical data to public cloud providers, compliance with local privacy regulations (such as LGPD or national data protection laws) is mandatory.",
        "**• Data Sovereignty:** Guarantees customer data is stored and processed exclusively within specified geographic cloud regions.",
        "**• Key Sovereignty (CMEK):** Customer-Managed Encryption Keys allow organizations to retain full cryptographic ownership over their data at rest and in transit.",
        "**• Operational Sovereignty:** Restricts cloud provider support personnel access unless explicitly authorized by the client."
      ]
    },
    section3: {
      heading: "3. Example: Programmatic Audit Log Inspection with GCP SDK",
      paragraphs: [
        `In automated **DevSecOps & CI/CD pipelines** *(if you'd like to read about the challenges of deployment pipelines, check out my <a href="/en/blog-deployment" class="inline-blog-link">entry on deployments</a>)*, security telemetry can be ingested and filtered programmatically using cloud audit logs:`
      ],
      codeLabel: "Node.js Audit Log Security Event Filter",
      code: `import { Logging } from '@google-cloud/logging';

const logging = new Logging({ projectId: 'jill-sec-audit' });

async function streamSecurityEvents() {
  const log = logging.log('cloudaudit.googleapis.com%2Factivity');
  
  // Filter for IAM policy alterations or unusual admin actions
  const filter = 'resource.type="gce_instance" AND protoPayload.methodName="v1.compute.instances.insert"';
  const [entries] = await log.getEntries({ filter, pageSize: 10 });

  entries.forEach(entry => {
    console.log(\`[ALERT] Security Activity by \${entry.metadata.protoPayload?.authenticationInfo?.principalEmail}\`);
  });
}

streamSecurityEvents();`
    },
    section4: {
      heading: "4. Practical Trade-offs in Security Automation",
      paragraphs: [
        "**Benefits:** Faster incident response, automated threat triage, and reduced manual log auditing overhead.",
        "**Trade-offs:** AI-generated security recommendations must always be validated by human SecOps/DevOps engineers before executing automated infrastructure remediations to avoid accidental downtime."
      ]
    }
  },
  es: {
    title: "Ciberseguridad e IA en la Nube — Automatización con SecLM y Soberanía Digital",
    date: "4 de Octubre, 2026",
    subtitle: "El diario de desarrollo de Jill",
    back: 'Volver al Inicio',
    intro: "Una revisión técnica sobre el uso de modelos de IA especializados en seguridad (SecLM) y los esquemas de soberanía digital en la nube.",
    introDesc: "Análisis práctico sobre detección automatizada de amenazas, triaje de logs y cumplimiento de residencia de datos.",
    introExtra: [
      "SecLM es un modelo de lenguaje afinado con inteligencia de amenazas de Mandiant y telemetría de seguridad de Google.",
      "La soberanía digital garantiza que los datos permanezcan dentro de jurisdicciones geográficas específicas según normativas locales."
    ],
    section1: {
      heading: "1. IA aplicada a Ciberseguridad: ¿Qué es SecLM?",
      paragraphs: [
        "Los entornos cloud modernos generan millones de eventos de seguridad y registros diarios. Las herramientas SIEM tradicionales dependen de reglas estáticas que suelen generar alto volumen de falsos positivos.",
        `**SecLM (Security Language Model)** es un modelo de IA especializado entrenado en informes de amenazas, comportamiento de código malicioso y configuraciones de seguridad *(si quieres aprender sobre la privacidad y ejecución de modelos locales, revisa mi <a href="/es/blog-hermes" class="inline-blog-link">análisis de IAs locales</a>)*.`,
        "En **Security AI Command Center**, SecLM resume vectores de ataque complejos en lenguaje claro y sugiere comandos de remediación."
      ]
    },
    section2: {
      heading: "2. Soberanía Digital y Residencia de Datos",
      paragraphs: [
        "Para empresas y organismos que mueven datos sensibles a la nube, el cumplimiento de regulaciones locales de privacidad es un requisito indispensable:",
        "**• Soberanía de Datos:** Garantiza que la información se almacene y procese exclusivamente en regiones geográficas delimitadas.",
        "**• Soberanía de Claves (CMEK):** Permite a la organización mantener el control criptográfico total sobre sus claves de cifrado en reposo y en tránsito.",
        "**• Soberanía Operativa:** Restringe el acceso del personal de soporte del proveedor de nube a menos que sea explícitamente autorizado."
      ]
    },
    section3: {
      heading: "3. Ejemplo de Inspección Programática de Logs de Auditoría",
      paragraphs: [
        `En **pipelines automatizados de CI/CD** *(si quieres recordar los retos del despliegue en producción, consulta mi <a href="/es/blog-deployment" class="inline-blog-link">entrada sobre el miedo al deploy</a>)*, la telemetría de seguridad se puede consultar programáticamente para detectar alteraciones de configuración:`
      ],
      codeLabel: "Filtro de Eventos de Seguridad en Node.js",
      code: `import { Logging } from '@google-cloud/logging';

const logging = new Logging({ projectId: 'jill-sec-audit' });

async function streamSecurityEvents() {
  const log = logging.log('cloudaudit.googleapis.com%2Factivity');
  
  // Filtrar cambios en políticas de IAM o creación no autorizada de recursos
  const filter = 'resource.type="gce_instance" AND protoPayload.methodName="v1.compute.instances.insert"';
  const [entries] = await log.getEntries({ filter, pageSize: 10 });

  entries.forEach(entry => {
    console.log(\`[ALERTA] Evento de Seguridad por \${entry.metadata.protoPayload?.authenticationInfo?.principalEmail}\`);
  });
}

streamSecurityEvents();`
    },
    section4: {
      heading: "4. Consideraciones Técnicas",
      paragraphs: [
        "**Beneficios:** Mayor velocidad en el triaje de incidentes y reducción del trabajo manual en análisis de logs.",
        "**Consideraciones:** Las recomendaciones de remediación generadas por IA deben ser auditadas por ingenieros de seguridad antes de aplicarse en producción."
      ]
    }
  },
  pt: {
    title: "Cibersegurança e IA na Nuvem — Automação com SecLM e Soberania Digital",
    date: "4 de Outubro, 2026",
    subtitle: "O diário de desenvolvimento de Jill",
    back: 'Voltar ao Início',
    intro: "Análise técnica do uso de IA especializada em segurança (SecLM) e soberania de dados na nuvem.",
    introDesc: "Visão prática sobre detecção de ameaças, logs de auditoria e conformidade regulatória.",
    introExtra: [
      "SecLM é um modelo especializado treinado em relatórios de inteligência de ameaças.",
      "A soberania digital assegura que os dados permaneçam sob controle geográfico e regulatório local."
    ],
    section1: {
      heading: "1. O que é o SecLM?",
      paragraphs: [
        `O **SecLM** é um modelo de IA treinado para identificar padrões de ataque em registros de auditoria *(se quiser entender modelos locais, confira meu <a href="/pt/blog-hermes" class="inline-blog-link">post sobre IAs locais</a>)* e sugerir ações de remediação.`
      ]
    },
    section2: {
      heading: "2. Soberania Digital e Criptografia",
      paragraphs: [
        "**• Residência de Dados:** Garantia de armazenamento em regiões específicas.",
        "**• Chaves CMEK:** Controle total do cliente sobre as chaves de criptografia."
      ]
    },
    section3: {
      heading: "3. Inspeção Programática de Logs de Auditoria",
      paragraphs: [
        `Exemplo de código para monitorar eventos em **pipelines de CI/CD** *(relembre os desafios no meu <a href="/pt/blog-deployment" class="inline-blog-link">post sobre deploy</a>)*:`
      ],
      codeLabel: "Filtro de Logs de Auditoria em Node.js",
      code: `import { Logging } from '@google-cloud/logging';

const logging = new Logging({ projectId: 'jill-sec-audit' });

async function streamSecurityEvents() {
  const log = logging.log('cloudaudit.googleapis.com%2Factivity');
  const filter = 'resource.type="gce_instance" AND protoPayload.methodName="v1.compute.instances.insert"';
  const [entries] = await log.getEntries({ filter, pageSize: 10 });

  entries.forEach(entry => {
    console.log(\`[ALERTA] Evento: \${entry.metadata.protoPayload?.authenticationInfo?.principalEmail}\`);
  });
}

streamSecurityEvents();`
    },
    section4: {
      heading: "4. Considerações Finais",
      paragraphs: [
        "Recomendações automáticas de IA devem passar por validação de engenheiros antes da aplicação em produção."
      ]
    }
  }
};

const c = content[lang] || content.es;
---

<Layout title={`${c.title} | Jill Portfolio`} lang={lang}>
  <Animations client:load />
  
  <div class="blog-post-page">
    <Nav activeSection="blog" lang={lang} />
    
    <main class="container">
      <article class="post-article">
        <a href={`/${lang}/#blog`} class="back-link">
          <span class="arrow">←</span> {c.back}
        </a>

        <header class="post-header">
          <div class="meta-badge">
            Cloud Security & Governance
          </div>
          <h1 class="post-title">{c.title}</h1>
          <p class="post-subtitle">{c.subtitle}</p>
          <div class="post-date">
            <span class="calendar-icon">📅</span> {c.date}
          </div>
        </header>

        <div class="post-card">
          <section class="intro-section">
            <div class="intro-bubble">
              <p class="intro-main">{c.intro}</p>
              <p class="intro-desc">{c.introDesc}</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="extra-bullets">
              {c.introExtra.map(bullet => (
                <div class="bullet-item">
                  <span class="bullet-icon">•</span>
                  <span>{bullet}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>

          <hr class="divider" />

          <section class="content-section">
            <h2 class="section-heading">{c.section1.heading}</h2>
            {c.section1.paragraphs.map(p => (
              <p class="section-paragraph" set:html={p.replace(/\*\*(.*?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>')} />
            ))}
          </section>

          <section class="content-section">
            <h2 class="section-heading">{c.section2.heading}</h2>
            {c.section2.paragraphs.map(p => (
              <p class="section-paragraph" set:html={p.replace(/\*\*(.*?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>')} />
            ))}
          </section>

          <section class="content-section">
            <h2 class="section-heading">{c.section3.heading}</h2>
            {c.section3.paragraphs.map(p => (
              <p class="section-paragraph" set:html={p.replace(/\*\*(.*?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>')} />
            ))}

            <div class="code-box">
              <div class="code-header">
                <span class="code-dot red"></span>
                <span class="code-dot yellow"></span>
                <span class="code-dot green"></span>
                <span class="code-title">{c.section3.codeLabel}</span>
              </div>
              <pre class="code-block"><code>{c.section3.code}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="content-section conclusion-box">
            <h2 class="section-heading">{c.section4.heading}</h2>
            {c.section4.paragraphs.map(p => (
              <p class="section-paragraph" set:html={p.replace(/\*\*(.*?)\*\*/g, '<strong>$1</strong>')} />
            ))}
          </section>

          <section class="comments-wrapper">
            <CommentsSection client:load postSlug="blog-security-ai" currentLang={lang} />
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-post-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at top center, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1) 0%, rgba(15, 15, 26, 0.98) 70%);
    color: #e2e8f0;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: #38bdf8;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: #0284c7;
    transform: translateX(-4px);
  }

  .post-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .meta-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 1rem;
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.25);
    border-radius: 9999px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: #38bdf8;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .post-title {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.25;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffffff 0%, #cbd5e1 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .post-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .post-date {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: #cbd5e1;
  }

  .post-card {
    background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }

  .intro-bubble {
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08);
    border-left: 4px solid #38bdf8;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .intro-main {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #f8fafc;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .intro-desc {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .extra-bullets {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .bullet-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .bullet-icon {
    color: #38bdf8;
  }

  .divider {
    border: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3), transparent);
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .section-heading {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #f8fafc;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .section-paragraph {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #cbd5e1;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  :global(.inline-blog-link) {
    color: #38bdf8;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }
  :global(.inline-blog-link:hover) {
    color: #7dd3fc;
  }

  .code-box {
    background: #0f172a;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .code-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  }

  .code-dot {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .code-dot.red { background: #ef4444; }
  .code-dot.yellow { background: #eab308; }
  .code-dot.green { background: #22c55e; }

  .code-title {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-family: monospace;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
  }

  .code-block {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: 'Fira Code', 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #38bdf8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .conclusion-box {
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    padding: 1.75rem;
  }

  .comments-wrapper {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .post-title {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }
    .post-card {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
